          "content": "MATHEMATICS"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.162,
            0.143,
            0.671,
            0.179
          ],
          "content": "\\left( \\mathrm{ix} \\right) \\left( \\mathrm{c o s e c A} - \\sin \\mathrm{A} \\right) \\left( \\mathrm{s e c A} - \\cos \\mathrm{A} \\right) = \\frac{1}{\\tan \\mathrm{A} + \\cot \\mathrm{A}}",
          "image_source": "images/page_19_equation_2.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.203,
            0.187,
            0.567,
            0.205
          ],
          "content": "**[Hint : Simplify LHS and RHS separately]**"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.205,
            0.213,
            0.543,
            0.26
          ],
          "content": "\\left( \\frac{1 + \\tan^{2} A}{1 + \\cot^{2} A} \\right) = \\left( \\frac{1 - \\tan A}{1 - \\cot A} \\right)^{2} = \\tan^{2} A",
          "image_source": "images/page_19_equation_4.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.098,
            0.274,
            0.252,
            0.293
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "8.5 Summary"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.097,
            0.301,
            0.579,
            0.318
          ],
          "content": "**In this chapter, you have studied the following points :**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.124,
            0.323,
            0.518,
            0.341
          ],
          "content": "**1. In a right triangle ABC, right-angled at B,**"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.154,
            0.344,
            0.754,
            0.383
          ],
          "content": "\\sin \\mathrm{A}=\\frac{\\text { side opposite to angle A}}{\\text { hypotemuse }}, \\cos \\mathrm{A}=\\frac{\\text { side adjacent to angle A}}{\\text { hypotemuse }}",
          "image_source": "images/page_19_equation_8.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.154,
            0.387,
            0.457,
            0.426
          ],
          "content": "side opposite to angle A **tan A =** side adjacent to angle A"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.124,
            0.427,
            0.758,
            0.465
          ],
          "content": "**2.**cosec $\\mathrm { A } = { \\frac { 1 } { \\sin \\mathrm { A } } } ;$ sec $\\mathrm { A } = { \\frac { 1 } { \\cos \\mathrm { A } } }$ ; tan $\\mathrm{A} \\rightrightarrows \\frac{\\mathrm{A}}{\\cot \\mathrm{A}}$ ,  tan $\\mathrm{A} \\geq \\frac{\\sin \\mathrm{A}_{i}}{\\cos \\mathrm{A}}$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.123,
            0.465,
            0.9,
            0.5
          ],
          "content": "**3. If one of the trigonometric ratios of an acute angle is known, the remaining trigonometric ratios of the angle can be easily determined.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.124,
            0.503,
            0.754,
            0.521
          ],
          "content": "4. The values of trigonometric ratios for angles $0^{\\circ},30^{\\circ},45^{\\circ},60^{\\circ}$ and $9 0 ^ { \\circ }$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.124,
            0.524,
            0.9,
            0.559
          ],
          "content": "**5. The value of sin A or cos A never exceeds 1, whereas the value of sec A** $( 0 ^ { \\circ } \\leq \\mathrm { A } < 9 0 ^ { \\circ } )$ **or cosec** $\\mathrm{A}(0^{\\circ}<\\mathrm{A} \\leq 90^{\\circ})$ **is always greater than or equal to 1.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.125,
            0.562,
            0.322,
            0.578
          ],
          "content": "**6. sin**<strong><sup>2</sup></strong> $A + \\cos^{2}A = 1$ **,**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.155,
            0.582,
            0.475,
            0.599
          ],
          "content": "se $\\mathrm{c}^{2} \\mathrm{A}-\\tan ^{2} \\mathrm{A}=1$ **for** $0 ^ { \\circ } \\leq \\mathrm { A } < 9 0 ^ { \\circ }$ **,**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.155,
            0.602,
            0.495,
            0.619
          ],
          "content": "cosec $^{2}\\mathrm{A}=1+\\cot^{2}\\mathrm{A}$ **for** $0^{\\circ} <  A  \\leq 90^{\\circ}$ **.**"
        },
